  "_README": [
    "TAXI FARES.",
    "",
    "Every number here was lifted verbatim from the 'gettingThere' lines in",
    "areas.json and the cruise guides — Josh's own copy, already shipping in",
    "the app. Nothing was sourced from the web: taxi fares online are forum",
    "posts and fare-estimator sites that disagree with each other, and a",
    "wrong number here costs someone money at the roadside.",
    "",
    "One exception: Town Center port to West Bay is $10-15, not the $8-12",
    "the area guide used to say. Josh corrected it, and areas.json was",
    "changed to match. He lives here; he outranks the file.",
    "",
    "A fare is only recorded in the SHARED column where the original copy",
    "said '/person'. Where it didn't, the fare is left null rather than",
    "guessed into a column — telling colectivo from private is the entire",
    "point of this screen, and putting a per-car price in the per-person",
    "column would do more harm than showing nothing.",
    "",
    "  colectivoUSD     low end, US dollars PER PERSON in a shared taxi",
    "  colectivoMaxUSD  top of the range. null when the fare is one number.",
    "  privateUSD       low end, US dollars for the WHOLE CAR",
    "  privateMaxUSD    top of that range",
    "  note             anything that changes the number",
    "",
    "STILL UNKNOWN, and the routes visitors ask about most: everything from",
    "the airport, West End to West Bay by road, and both private-car",
    "columns. The guides quote airport→West Bay at $15-20 and Coxen",
    "Hole→Oak Ridge at $20-25 without saying whether that is per person or",
    "per car, so those are sitting here as nulls until someone who knows",
    "says which.",
    "",
    "A route with both fares null never renders, and the screen hides",
    "entirely if no route has one. This file is safe to ship half-filled."
  ],

